---
import Layout from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
export const prerender = false;
---
<Layout
  title={`Terms of Use — ${SITE.title}`}
  description={`Terms and conditions for using ${SITE.name}.`}
>
  <nav class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a> › <span>Terms of Use</span>
  </nav>
  <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
  <p>Last updated: 21 September 2026</p>
  <p>
    By using {SITE.url} ("the site"), you agree to these terms.
    If you do not agree, please stop using the site.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What the site is</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is an informational directory of Indian pincodes, villages,
    and panchayats, assembled from public data sources.
  </p>

  <h2>2. No warranty of accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to keep data correct, but it is provided "as is" without
    warranty of any kind. Pincode boundaries, village names, and local body
    codes change over time. Always confirm critical details (postal address,
    official codes) with India Post or the concerned government office before
    submitting documents.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Permitted use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You may browse, search, and link to the site freely</li>
    <li>Automated scraping, bulk downloading, or republishing of the directory is not allowed without written permission</li>
    <li>You may not use the site in any way that overloads or disrupts it</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Site design, organisation, and written content belong to SKM Studio Network.
    Underlying public data belongs to its respective government sources.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    We are not liable for any loss or damage arising from use of, or reliance
    on, the information on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may change these terms or the site's features at any time. Continued use
    of the site means you accept the updated terms. Questions?
    <a href="/contact">Contact us</a>.
  </p>
</Layout>
